{
  "id": "typescript-15-recursive-types",
  "slug": "recursive-types",
  "title": "Recursive types and depth limits",
  "moduleId": "typescript-15-advanced-type-patterns",
  "order": 2,
  "hook": "**Recursive types** model JSON trees and ASTs: `type Json = string | Json[] | { [k: string]: Json }`. Compiler depth limits cause TS2589 on deep mapped recursion.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Type references itself. **Json** union canonical. **interface** for trees often cleaner. **Depth-limited** DeepPartial prevents TS2589. Runtime validation still required — types erase."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "recursive",
              "longForm": "self-reference",
              "plainDefinition": "Type includes itself.",
              "example": "type Tree<T> = { v: T; c: Tree<T>[] }"
            },
            {
              "term": "TS2589",
              "longForm": "excessively deep",
              "plainDefinition": "Compiler depth limit.",
              "example": "unbounded mapped recursion"
            },
            {
              "term": "Json",
              "longForm": "JSONValue",
              "plainDefinition": "Standard recursive JSON type.",
              "example": "string|number|Json[]|{...}"
            },
            {
              "term": "zod lazy",
              "longForm": "runtime recursive schema",
              "plainDefinition": "Matches recursive type at boundary.",
              "example": "z.lazy(() => schema)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "API trees, AST, config. DeepPartial<Json> blows budget. Interview JSON + depth question."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: infinite expansion",
          "body": "Unbounded mapped recursion on Json → TS2589 — add depth param."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "base + recursive arm",
              "body": "union self-ref"
            },
            {
              "title": "interface for trees",
              "body": "Node { children: Node[] }"
            },
            {
              "title": "watch depth",
              "body": "simplify conditionals"
            },
            {
              "title": "runtime validate",
              "body": "zod lazy"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Json recursion",
            "source": "flowchart TD\n  J --> P[primitives]\n  J --> A[Json[]]\n  J --> O[{string:Json}]\n  A --> J\n  O --> J"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Json type",
            "code": "type Json = string | number | boolean | null | Json[] | { [key: string]: Json };\nfunction parseJson(t: string): Json { return JSON.parse(t) as Json; }",
            "explanation": "Canonical pattern — add runtime validator in prod."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "AST interface",
            "code": "interface Expr { kind: \"lit\" | \"add\"; value?: number; left?: Expr; right?: Expr; }",
            "explanation": "Interface recursive node."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Depth-limited DeepPartial",
            "code": "type DP<T, D extends number = 5> = D extends 0 ? T : T extends object ? { [K in keyof T]?: DP<T[K], [-1,0,1,2,3,4][D]> } : T;",
            "explanation": "Depth counter prevents blow-up."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: unbounded",
            "code": "// type Bad<T> = { [K in keyof T]: Bad<T[K]> } on Json → TS2589",
            "explanation": "Need depth or stop at primitives."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
